1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,960
One appointment. One date. Can you finish it using
only a keyboard?

2
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:12,500
You press Tab. Focus skips the date control. The
page loads, but the booking is still blocked.

3
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:20,760
This is AccessFinish. It helps developers review an
AI source repair, then check whether the intended
task actually succeeds.

4
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:27,260
For this guided Easy!Appointments case, we supplied
the diagnosis and repair direction.

5
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:36,300
NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super, running on Nebius Token
Factory, proposed five source edits. The request and
response are retained.

6
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:44,960
First, inspect the change. The date control becomes
keyboard editable. Calendar refreshes must preserve
the typed date.

7
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:48,080
Approval is bound to this exact patch hash.

8
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:56,500
Then execute the recorded proposal in a fresh,
isolated fixture. Build the application. Complete
the keyboard booking.

9
00:00:56,580 --> 00:01:03,060
Check storage through a separate read-only database
reader. Reopen the appointment in a fresh browser.

10
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:14,360
Here is the payoff. November 2, 2026. Nine to nine
thirty, Riyadh time. The expected booking was saved
and independently reopened.

11
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:18,680
Existing data and the regression controls also
passed.

12
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:26,780
But a convincing patch is not enough. Another
attempt completed the keyboard task, then failed the
calendar control.

13
00:01:26,860 --> 00:01:28,780
AccessFinish rejected it.

14
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:38,160
Across five frozen attempts on this one guided case,
two passed completely. Two failed to build. One
failed a regression check.

15
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:44,880
Every failure is retained. Broader repair accuracy
and screen-reader validation remain open.

16
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:52,420
For developers and accessibility QA, the question is
simple: did the user finish the task, with the right
data?

17
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:57,000
AccessFinish. Review the repair. Verify the outcome.
